{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CesXxQith2rEo4YMQWBUV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have enough information for the analysis phase. Let me summarize:\n\n**Repository findings (cited with line numbers):**\n- ShipmentController.kt:22-24 - RestController with ShipmentRepository injection\n- ShipmentRepository.kt:15-18 - save() persists by shipmentId\n- ShipmentRepository.kt:22 - findById() retrieves or returns null\n- Shipment.kt:9-14 - data class with immutable status field\n- ApiExceptions.kt:18-24 - ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409) classes\n- ApiError.kt:31-37 - ErrorCode enum (currently no code for cancelled state conflicts)\n\n**Conventions this repository follows:**\n1. Controllers throw ApiException subclasses; GlobalExceptionHandler converts them to ApiError responses\n2. 404 errors use ResourceNotFoundException with ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND (ShipmentController.kt:49-52)\n3. 409 errors use ConflictException with ErrorCode (e.g., ShipmentController.kt:29)\n4. POST endpoints return ResponseEntity with HttpStatus (ShipmentController.kt:43, OrderController.kt:33)\n5. Repository pattern: get by ID, check state, throw if invalid, save updated entity\n6. Tests use @SpringBootTest with MockMvc, verify status codes and JSON paths (ShipmentControllerTest.kt)\n\n**Affected files (cannot be avoided):**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` - Must add the POST confirm endpoint\n2. `ApiError.kt` - Must add ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED for the 409 case\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - Must add tests for confirm functionality\n\n**Risks:**\n1. Shipment is immutable; confirming requires creating a new instance (data class copy mechanism)\n2. Need to handle the idempotent case correctly (no-op for already-confirmed)\n3. New ErrorCode must not conflict with future requirements\n4. The in-memory store uses ConcurrentHashMap so updates must go through save()\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone - all cases in the requirement are clearly specified.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** - Add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED` error code to the ErrorCode enum. This will be used when attempting to confirm a CANCELLED shipment.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** - Add a new endpoint `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` that:\n   - Retrieves the shipment by ID, throwing ResourceNotFoundException if not found (404)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throws ConflictException with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED (409)\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, returns the existing shipment unchanged (idempotent)\n   - If status is CREATED, updates it to CONFIRMED, saves it, and returns the updated shipment\n   - Returns ResponseEntity with OK status (200) containing the shipment\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add four test cases:\n   - Confirms a CREATED shipment moves it to CONFIRMED\n   - Confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds without error\n   - Confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 Conflict\n   - Confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 Not Found\n\n**Rejected alternatives:**\n\n1. **Add a new exception type** (e.g., CancelledShipmentException) - Rejected because ConflictException already handles 409 errors and using a new exception type would be inconsistent with how ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS uses the same ConflictException.\n\n2. **Use SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE or INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION** - Rejected because SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED is more explicit about what went wrong (confirming when cancelled), matching the clarity of SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS.\n\n3. **Return 200 with no body on idempotent confirm** - Rejected because the requirement says \"succeeds and changes nothing\" and the pattern in this codebase is to return the resource, which makes the state visible to the caller.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Flow | Response |\n|------|------|-------|------|----------|\n| Confirm CREATED → CONFIRMED | findById(id) | save(Shipment with CONFIRMED) | POST handler: fetch, check status, update, save, return | 200 OK + Shipment JSON |\n| Confirm CONFIRMED (idempotent) | findById(id) | (none) | POST handler: fetch, status is CONFIRMED, return as-is | 200 OK + Shipment JSON |\n| Confirm CANCELLED | findById(id) | (none) | POST handler: fetch, status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException | 409 Conflict + error envelope |\n| Confirm non-existent | (not found) | (none) | POST handler: fetch returns null, throw ResourceNotFoundException | 404 Not Found + error envelope |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n- Test 1: Happy path - creates shipment in CREATED, confirms it, verifies status changed to CONFIRMED\n- Test 2: Idempotent - confirms same shipment twice, verifies second call succeeds with no error\n- Test 3: Cancelled conflict - manually saves CANCELLED shipment to repository, attempts confirm, verifies 409 with correct error code\n- Test 4: Not found - attempts to confirm non-existent shipmentId, verifies 404 with correct error code\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1373,"cache_read_input_tokens":14928,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1373},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6edb97ea-277b-4b68-96ef-0c9bdbad94a0","uuid":"97cf6127-0e50-4dfc-890f-1a4a974460fc","timestamp":"2026-09-09T08:16:49.676Z","request_id":"req_011CesXxQ3T5WJWCkaZdwAmy"}
